                            <comment id="496417" author="adilger" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2026 05:38:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It looks like this failure was introduced by patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/56112&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56112&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18154&quot; title=&quot;Client can permanently hang in lustre recovery on race condition in replay_locks &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18154&quot;&gt;LU-18154&lt;/a&gt; ptlrpc: don&apos;t delay rq_no_delay after IDLE&quot;).  It failed once in the same way before landing, then failed several times in master-next before in landed on 2026-06-13 and started failing regularly on master. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496419" author="adilger" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2026 05:45:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ropermar&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ropermar&quot;&gt;ropermar&lt;/a&gt; could you please take a look into these failures. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I will push a revert patch, but you are also welcome to push a fix patch if it can be done quickly. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496423" author="adilger" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2026 06:01:29 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It looks like this might just be a test script issue that could be fixed by making the test more robust. I didn&apos;t realize originally that test_170 was added by the patch in question, but it may be racy when the timing of the recovery is not matching the expectations of the checks at the end (eg. if recovery is completed very quickly).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496441" author="aboyko" created="Fri, 19 Jun 2026 14:53:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I added a test with a fix, will take a look. Unfortunately not reproducible on my side. And Maloo logs are empy.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
